---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import legal from '../data/legal.json';

const months = ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', 'July',
  'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'];
const [y, m, d] = legal.lastUpdated.split('-').map(Number);
const updated = `${d} ${months[m - 1]} ${y}`;

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Privacy notice',
  url: `${site.domain}/privacy/`,
  dateModified: legal.lastUpdated,
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', url: site.domain, name: site.brand },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: site.legalName, url: site.domain },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice | Ruibit Power"
  description="What personal data Ruibit Power collects through ruibitpower.com, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and the rights you have under the GDPR."
  breadcrumbLabel="Privacy"
  structuredData={schema}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
    <p>
      What personal data this website collects, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and what
      you can ask us to do with it. Written to meet Article 13 of the EU General Data Protection
      Regulation.
    </p>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="article-body">
      <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName} (“Ruibit Power”, “we”) is the controller for the personal data described
        in this notice. We decide why and how that data is processed.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Postal address: {site.address}</li>
        <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
        <li>Telephone: {site.phone}</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We have not appointed a data protection officer, because our processing does not meet the
        thresholds in Article 37. Privacy questions and requests go to the email address above and
        are handled by the person responsible for commercial operations.
      </p>
      {
        legal.euRepresentative && (
          <p>
            Our representative in the European Union, designated under Article 27 GDPR, is{' '}
            {legal.euRepresentative}.
          </p>
        )
      }

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When you send an enquiry.</strong> The form on our contact page asks for your name,
        work email address, company, country, application type, target power in kW, target energy in
        kWh, required backup duration, and a free-text message. Fields marked as required must be
        completed for us to answer; everything else is optional. The form is submitted to, and
        stored by, our hosting provider on our behalf.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you simply browse.</strong> Our hosting provider records standard server log
        data for every request: IP address, browser user agent, the page requested, and a timestamp.
        This is used for security, capacity planning, and diagnosing faults. We do not build
        profiles from it and we do not combine it with enquiry data.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What we do not collect.</strong> This website sets no cookies, runs no analytics, no
        advertising, and no session recording. There are no tracking pixels and no embedded players
        that load before you click. See section 7.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we use it, and on what legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>To answer your enquiry and prepare a quotation</strong> — Article 6(1)(b) GDPR,
          processing necessary to take steps at your request before entering into a contract.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To keep records of quotations, orders, and warranty claims</strong> — Article
          6(1)(b), and Article 6(1)(c) where accounting or tax law requires us to retain documents.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To keep the website available and secure</strong> — Article 6(1)(f), our legitimate
          interest in protecting the site against abuse and in diagnosing faults. We keep this to
          what is necessary for that purpose.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To send you commercial email</strong> — only with your prior consent under Article
          6(1)(a), which you give separately and can withdraw at any time. A quotation in response
          to your enquiry is not marketing and does not depend on consent.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiries that do not lead to an order</strong> — {legal.enquiryRetentionMonths}{' '}
          months from the last exchange, then deleted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Records relating to an order</strong> — for as long as the contract and warranty
          run, and afterwards for the period required by the accounting and tax law that applies to
          us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Server logs</strong> — {legal.logRetentionMonths} months.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Where we keep data because a law requires it, we restrict access to that data to the purpose
        the law demands and stop using it for anything else.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it for advertising.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong> — website hosting and form handling. Netlify stores form
          submissions on our behalf and processes them under a data processing agreement.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Our email provider</strong> — to receive and answer enquiries.
        </li>
        {
          legal.sharesWithManufacturingPartner && (
            <li>
              <strong>{site.manufacturingPartner.replace(/\.+$/, '')}</strong> — our manufacturing
              partner. Where an enquiry needs factory input on configuration, certification, lead
              time, or price, we pass the technical and commercial details needed to answer it. We
              do not pass data that is not needed for that purpose, and the partner is bound to use
              it only for the enquiry.
            </li>
          )
        }
        <li>
          <strong>Professional advisers and authorities</strong> — where we are legally required to
          disclose, or where it is necessary to establish or defend a legal claim.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Transfers outside the European Economic Area</h2>
      <p>
        We are established in China and our hosting and email providers process data in the United
        States. Where personal data of a person in the EEA is transferred outside it, the transfer
        relies on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses in the provider's data
        processing agreement, together with the technical and organisational measures described in
        section 9. You can ask us for a copy of the relevant safeguards using the contact details in
        section 1.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">7. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>This website sets no cookies.</strong> There is no analytics package, no advertising
        tag, no tag manager, and no social media pixel on any page.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The WhatsApp button and the social media icons in the footer are ordinary links. Nothing
          loads from those services, and no cookie is set, until you click one and leave this site.
        </li>
        <li>
          Fonts, stylesheets, scripts and images are served from this domain. No third-party content
          is embedded in our pages.
        </li>
        <li>
          The contact form is submitted directly to our hosting provider. It sets no cookie and
          stores nothing in your browser.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you choose a cookie preference through the settings link in our footer, that choice is
        stored in your own browser's local storage so we do not ask again. It is not transmitted to
        us and it is not used to identify you. You can clear it at any time through your browser
        settings, and the link in the footer lets you change it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we introduce analytics or any other non-essential technology in future, we will ask for
        your consent first and will not load it before you give that consent. This notice will be
        updated before that happens.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>be informed about how your data is used — this notice does that;</li>
        <li>obtain a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data erased where we no longer have a lawful reason to keep it;</li>
        <li>restrict how we use it while a question about accuracy or lawfulness is open;</li>
        <li>object to processing based on our legitimate interests;</li>
        <li>receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format, or have it sent to another controller;</li>
        <li>withdraw any consent you have given, without affecting processing carried out before you withdrew it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We answer
        within one month; if the request is complex we may extend that by two further months and will
        tell you why. We may ask for information to confirm your identity before acting, so that we
        do not disclose data to the wrong person.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority in the EU member
        state where you live, where you work, or where the alleged infringement happened. We would
        prefer the chance to resolve it with you first.
      </p>

      <h2>9. How we protect it</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served over HTTPS. Access to enquiry data is limited to the people who need it to
        answer you. Form submissions are held by our hosting provider in access-controlled systems,
        and our own copies are kept in accounts protected by multi-factor authentication. We keep the
        amount of data we collect to what the enquiry actually requires.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site sells industrial and residential energy storage equipment to businesses and
        professional buyers. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect data
        from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has submitted data, contact us and we will
        delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle personal data, we update this page and move the date at the top.
        Material changes that affect people we already hold data about are communicated by email
        where we have an address for them.
      </p>

      <h2>12. How to contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this notice, or about how your data is handled, go to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or by post to {site.legalName},{' '}
        {site.address}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
